1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:37,000
This is Agentic Game Studio. Type a sentence,
and a playable 3D game builds itself, live, in your browser.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:37,000
On the left, a real Muse Code agent works inside the VM terminal.
It researches the genre, writes a stage-by-stage build plan,
then executes it: architecture, assets, world, gameplay, audio, verification.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The sidebar holds your projects, resumable terminal sessions,
eight toggleable agent skills, and the full system-design pipeline.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Everything runs on Meta's AI stack. Muse Wonder designs the game.
Muse Spark enriches the assets. Muse Image paints the concept art.
Sam segments it, Sam 3D reconstructs it, and the Muse Code CLI assembles it all.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Judge builds execute inside a locked-down Google gVisor sandbox.
Every build must pass a zero-tolerance visual QA gate.

6
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Meet Mother Agatha — the stalker haunting our flagship game.
Segmented by Sam 3.1, bound to a twenty-bone Blender armature,
driven by baked idle and walk animations.

7
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Our flagship: a gothic stealth-horror game built from nineteen
real photogrammetry scans. A live Meta AI director whispers
tactics every fourteen seconds.

8
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Find the chapel key. Hide in the wardrobe. Unlock the chapel door.

9
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Nothing here is a claim without evidence. Type a sentence.
Play a 3D game. That is Agentic Game Studio.
